        <type>const int</type>
        <definition>const int ndxlInit</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlInit</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Initialises the NDXL library. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Initialises the library&apos;s internal variables and garbage collection.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>NDXL_OK.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>This function must be called before using any other NDXL functionality. Failure to initialise the library can lead to memory leaks, segmentation faults, and other memory-related errors.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Registers cleanup functions to be executed when the program terminates. These functions release NDXL-managed resources that have not been explicitly freed by the user.</para>
</simplesect>
External memory allocations, such as those made using malloc() or calloc(), remain the responsibility of the user, and must be freed explicitly. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
